<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziryab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 789–857</span> · Also known as Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Nafi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziryab, born Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Nafi, was a musician and singer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> who settled at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-ii">Abd al-Rahman II</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 822. Later tradition credits him with introducing eastern fashions in music, dress, hairstyles, cuisine and table manners to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, and with adding a fifth string to the oud. He is remembered as a founding figure of Andalusi musical culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziryab.jpg" alt="Ziryab" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Américo Toledano · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monumento_a_Ziryab_002.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
